WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.328
- Have a seat.

00:00:01.328 --> 00:00:04.229
(audience cheering)

00:00:04.229 --> 00:00:05.062
- Thank you.

00:00:05.062 --> 00:00:07.109
- Here's the thing.

00:00:07.109 --> 00:00:08.630
I don't know a ton about sports ball,

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.385
but I do know you and I grew up on you

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:12.480
and there are so many
Texans here right now,

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.470
in this crew,
(the crew and audience cheers)

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.770
that you might get tackled at some point.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:17.603
So just I'm giving you

00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:18.810
a heads up.
- That's okay, yeah.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:20.820
You're a Dallas girl.
- Yes, yes.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:22.870
I'm a Fort Worth, but yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:24.350
- Awesome.
- Exactly, we are.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:27.180
So wait, so you're not allowed
to say who will win the game.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.013
- Yeah.
- I know that, okay.

00:00:28.013 --> 00:00:28.846
(audience laughs)

00:00:28.846 --> 00:00:30.779
- Well, I'm allowed to,
but I'm not going to, yeah.

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:33.780
- Oh, okay, okay, so why?

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.040
- Well, I call these games.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.513
So I just, you know...

00:00:36.513 --> 00:00:38.691
- You feel like it's favoritism?

00:00:38.691 --> 00:00:40.290
- A little bit.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.280
- I try to be neutral.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.360
And I wanna get along with
all the fan bases, so...

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.193
- No, totally.

00:00:45.193 --> 00:00:46.026
But you think the Rams will win?

00:00:46.026 --> 00:00:47.059
- Well, I do like the Rams.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:49.370
I do like the Rams.
(audience cheering)

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.310
I do like the Rams and, you know,

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:53.530
Matthew Stafford, also a Dallas kid.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.363
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:56.560
- And you know, he played
ball right there where I live,

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:58.710
but Joe Burrow with the
Bengals and what they've done,

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.440
I think that's been great for the NFL.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:01.273
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:01:01.273 --> 00:01:03.810
- You know, the fan base hasn't,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.250
they haven't won a lot in Cincinnati,

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.410
so this has been fantastic.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.750
So I think it's gonna
be a great Super Bowl.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:08.583
(audience clapping)
- It would.

00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:10.640
I'm just saying, it would be pretty cool

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.640
to be hosting the Super Bowl,
and then win the Super Bowl.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.110
I'm just saying it'd be a good moment.

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:16.327
- It would be a great moment.
- [Kelly] I'm just saying.

00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:17.160
- It would be a great moment.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:17.993
- [Kelly] Throwing it out there.

00:01:17.993 --> 00:01:18.985
- Yes.

00:01:18.985 --> 00:01:19.890
- So wait, so I hear
that you're about to work

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:20.770
with Blake Shelton.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:21.820
- Yes.
- Okay.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:23.272
Well, do you want warnings,

00:01:23.272 --> 00:01:25.651
or do you need help or
advice, or...? (laughs)

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:26.940
- Well, I love..

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.620
You all seem, and I don't
wanna speak for you,

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.820
but you seem like brothers
and sisters on that show.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:33.792
The chemistry...
- We basically represent

00:01:33.792 --> 00:01:36.134
Oklahoma and Texas, always at odds.

00:01:36.134 --> 00:01:36.967
- Yeah.
- But yes.

00:01:36.967 --> 00:01:38.455
- And he's been..

00:01:38.455 --> 00:01:42.130
So, I'm putting on a music
festival in Henryetta, Oklahoma,

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:42.963
where I'm from.

00:01:42.963 --> 00:01:43.900
It is a small town.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.316
It's 4,000 people and
I've got a whole lineup.

00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:51.370
It's a one day event and I've
got a number of great artists,

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.440
but I needed an Oklahoma headliner.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.440
And so I've been around
Blake a couple of times.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.640
He did a United Way event

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.194
that I was a part of years ago in Dallas.

00:01:59.194 --> 00:02:00.027
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:00.027 --> 00:02:01.417
- I texted him and said,

00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:03.757
"Hey, Blake, I'm putting
on this music festival.

00:02:03.757 --> 00:02:05.617
"I need an Oklahoma headliner

00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:07.762
"and you're my number one choice."

00:02:07.762 --> 00:02:08.595
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:12.785
- And within 10 minutes, Kelly,
he replied back, "I'm in.

00:02:12.785 --> 00:02:13.618
"I'm in."
(audience clapping)

00:02:13.618 --> 00:02:14.451
- He's the nicest guy.

00:02:14.451 --> 00:02:17.765
- He has been unbelievable.

00:02:17.765 --> 00:02:18.598
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:18.598 --> 00:02:21.190
- So it's June 11th,
highwaytohenryetta.com,

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:22.370
If you wanna go to the show.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:23.750
- Highway to Henryetta,
that's catchy, okay.

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.130
- It's, yeah, it's fantastic.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:29.010
So, we're gonna put Henryetta on the map.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:29.843
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:02:29.843 --> 00:02:30.826
- And I say we,

00:02:30.826 --> 00:02:33.360
Blake Shelton is gonna
put Henryetta on the map

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.370
and I couldn't be happier.
(audience clapping)

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.980
- I know, we mess with each
other but he's the nicest guy.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:38.450
- The best.
- So I'm not shocked at all.

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.180
- He's been amazing.
- Yeah, yeah..

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:41.170
Don't tell him I said this, though.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.714
- I won't (laughs).

00:02:42.714 --> 00:02:44.115
- He doesn't watch my show, he won't know.

00:02:44.115 --> 00:02:46.744
(laughing)And if you're
watching, I'm lying.

00:02:46.744 --> 00:02:47.590
(both laughing)

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:49.080
So you also just launched, okay,

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.370
a new, low calorie beer.
- [Troy] Yeah.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:51.584
- It's called Eight.
- [Troy] Yeah.

00:02:51.584 --> 00:02:52.417
(audience clapping)

00:02:52.417 --> 00:02:53.656
- I feel like I need to test it.

00:02:53.656 --> 00:02:54.489
- [Troy] Yes.

00:02:54.489 --> 00:02:55.322
- I feel like that's what's gonna happen.

00:02:55.322 --> 00:02:56.155
- [Troy] Yes.

00:02:56.155 --> 00:02:56.988
- I feel like it's rude,

00:02:56.988 --> 00:02:59.027
if you bring alcohol and
I'm not gonna try, oh.

00:02:59.027 --> 00:02:59.910
(audience member laughing)

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:01.410
Here's the thing.
- How great is that?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.380
- Here's the thing, I'm
not usually a beer girl.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:04.470
That's really good.

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:05.303
- It's good, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:03:05.303 --> 00:03:06.410
(audience cheering)

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:08.270
It tastes clean.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.790
I don't know why that's
the word I'm saying,

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:10.910
but it tastes really nice.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.320
- Well, you know, I worked
for a beer distributor

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:15.950
when I was in college, and I
I've drank my share of beer

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.310
but I never imagined that
I'd be making my beer.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.090
But I met my now partners,
through a mutual friend

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:23.300
and we wanted to do a low carb beer.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.260
What's unique about Eight,

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:28.200
is that there's no
adjuncts and no fillers.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.560
- Which is awesome.
- Which is awesome.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.810
And it's the only widely
known available beer,

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.180
that I'm aware of, that
can stake that claim.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.970
No sugars, no corn.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.280
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- No syrup, you know...

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.160
- Maybe that's why it
tastes like really light

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.032
and it's fresh.

00:03:41.032 --> 00:03:43.300
- It's a hundred percent organic grains.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:46.191
I refer to it as a better-for-you beer.

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:47.024
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:03:47.024 --> 00:03:49.699
- I think Blake Sheldon
and I are gonna love it.

00:03:49.699 --> 00:03:51.260
(audience clapping)

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:53.191
- Well, he is a beer person (laughing).

00:03:53.191 --> 00:03:54.024
- (laughing) Yes he is.

00:03:54.024 --> 00:03:55.610
- [Kelly] He's like, he
likes beer and vodka.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.560
- [Troy] He has been sent some so, yeah.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.740
- Yeah, I'm sure he took it and drank it.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.371
(laughter)

00:04:01.371 --> 00:04:02.839
So wait, while I have you here,

00:04:02.839 --> 00:04:04.670
I should know how to throw football.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:06.970
Now, I feel like I
learned when I was a kid,

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:08.380
but I don't know if I'm doing it right.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.690
So since you're here,

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:12.570
and so I will have bragging
rights to all of my friends

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:13.590
and family.
- [Troy] Absolutely.

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:14.610
- Will you teach me?

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:15.443
- 100%.

00:04:15.443 --> 00:04:16.870
(audience cheering)
- Okay, okay.

00:04:16.870 --> 00:04:17.703
Okay, let's do it.

00:04:17.703 --> 00:04:18.870
Let's do it, I'm so excited.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.559
I think I know how, but I don't know.

00:04:22.559 --> 00:04:24.360
My first question..

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.920
These are gigantic.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:26.753
- They are?

00:04:26.753 --> 00:04:28.259
- I don't remember them being this...

00:04:28.259 --> 00:04:29.630
This is huge.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:30.530
Okay, wait.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.450
So I feel like, don't you have a...

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:33.510
See, you don't hold it...

00:04:33.510 --> 00:04:34.459
- [Troy] I hold it a little differently.

00:04:34.459 --> 00:04:35.790
- You hold yours differently.
- I hold it differently.

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:36.860
- Wait, why?

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.180
- It's just the way it's
always worked for me, but..

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.204
- [Kelly] You like the
texture on your hand?

00:04:40.204 --> 00:04:41.358
- You can't hold it the way I hold.

00:04:41.358 --> 00:04:42.740
- I heard you're supposed
to have your finger..

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:43.573
Is that right?
- Yeah.

00:04:43.573 --> 00:04:46.296
Normally most quarterbacks
would hold it more like this.

00:04:46.296 --> 00:04:47.129
- [Kelly] I can't, my hand is so small.

00:04:47.129 --> 00:04:48.870
- [Troy] We have three fingers on

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.690
the laces.
- [Kelly] The laces, yeah.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:52.000
- I barely have one.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.300
I hold it way back here
on the back of the ball.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:54.550
- Yeah, but look at your hand and mine.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:56.478
- [Troy] I got big hands.
- [Kelly] Yeah (laughing).

00:04:56.478 --> 00:04:57.311
- I got big hands.

00:04:57.311 --> 00:04:58.270
- You can say it, that's gigantic.

00:04:58.270 --> 00:04:59.430
So I can do that.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:00.800
I can't hold it in either way,

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:01.912
but how do you...

00:05:01.912 --> 00:05:02.961
Thought you were supposed to let it spin.

00:05:02.961 --> 00:05:04.181
- [Troy] I thought you were an athlete.

00:05:04.181 --> 00:05:05.570
- I'm totally an athlete.
- You don't spin.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.710
You know just throw it, spin it.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:08.871
- Spin it off the tips, right?

00:05:08.871 --> 00:05:09.704
- Yeah.
- Okay.

00:05:09.704 --> 00:05:12.221
- Now what's gonna be embarrassing
is if I miss and you hit.

00:05:12.221 --> 00:05:13.160
(laughter and cheering)

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.960
- Not for me (laughing).
- Cause I haven't..

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.500
I literally have not throw
a ball in quite a while.

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:19.580
- I am looking so forward to this.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.920
Oh gosh, there's no
way I'm gonna hit that.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.990
Are you good at carnival games? I'm not.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:24.823
- Not bad.

00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:25.656
- Okay, oh go ahead.

00:05:25.656 --> 00:05:28.107
- You want me to go?
- Yeah, go show me how.

00:05:28.107 --> 00:05:31.620
(tins clattering)
(audience cheering)

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:32.453
Oh my God.

00:05:33.493 --> 00:05:35.110
I feel like I should be able to get closer

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:36.320
but I'm gonna try from here,

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:37.466
here I go.
- Okay.

00:05:37.466 --> 00:05:40.723
- Okay, okay, okay, okay.
(drums rumbling)

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:44.296
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:05:44.296 --> 00:05:45.448
(tins clattering)
No, wait.

00:05:45.448 --> 00:05:46.457
- You did it, you did it (laughing).

00:05:47.438 --> 00:05:50.809
(cymbals clanging)
(audience cheering)

00:05:50.809 --> 00:05:52.750
- Troy Aikman everybody.
(audience clapping)

00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:53.583
- Thank you.

